  "title": "ToolApiV1dot5",
  "description": "K-09 Tool API v1.5, a minor version for the walking skeleton's turn (T-1142; DL-322; README 'v1.5'): Sam's first text from a new number (S1-01), whose reply is S1-02's question, the turn D-017's card and human test run end to end. It only adds to v1.4 (tool-api.v1.4.schema.json, frozen by T-053 and unchanged, referred to here, which refers to v1.3, v1.2, v1.1 and v1): every v1.4 definition named here is under its own name, the unchanged ones by reference; the changed ones (buildFrontier.response, closestEntries.request, closestEntries.response, gateAndCommit.request and the three exchanges that hold them) only take K-02 v1.1's context (../model/model.v1.1.schema.json) in place of K-02 v1's, whose one change is a door value, signUp, the door to S1-01. So every v1 to v1.4 exchange is a v1.5 exchange. Added: no call, no key and no rule; the fixtures of the skeleton's turn 1 (build-frontier-s1-01.json, commit-s1-01.json), which turn 2's S1-02 fixtures (v1) stood in for. Each call's read, repeat and time budget are v1's (README 'Reads, repeats and time budgets'). Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
